{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-86918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X>8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-86918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =P(8<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3}{x}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-86918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd137fb13c4de7a3a10ea700653d2b85fdac1868d67f8ad33b94810ded43f3e3"} {"question" "q-86918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-86918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-86918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-87240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{6x},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-87240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{6x}$ on the interval $-\\infty <x\\le 0,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x={[\\frac{k}{6}{e}^{6x}]}_{-\\infty }^{0}=\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{6}=1\\,⟹\\,k=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-87240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd137fb13c4de7a3a10ea700653d2b85fdac1868d67f8ad33b94810ded43f3e3"} {"question" "q-87240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-87240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-87240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-126028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X>4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-126028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =P(4<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}]}_{4}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-126028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd137fb13c4de7a3a10ea700653d2b85fdac1868d67f8ad33b94810ded43f3e3"} {"question" "q-126028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-126028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-126028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}}$ on the interval $x\\ge 2,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{k}{2(2x-1)}\\,{|}_{2}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{6}=1\\,⟹\\,k=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd137fb13c4de7a3a10ea700653d2b85fdac1868d67f8ad33b94810ded43f3e3"} {"question" "q-160464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{3x+2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{3x+2}$ on the interval $x\\le 0,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{k}{3}{e}^{3x+2}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0}=\\frac{k{e}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k{e}^{2}}{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd137fb13c4de7a3a10ea700653d2b85fdac1868d67f8ad33b94810ded43f3e3"} {"question" "q-160467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072016/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b1d627fa755b92c18f7adca3b09789527534cdb478b845c51f81140d180964a"} {"question" "q-160467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3e"] ["math" "3{e}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{e}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{e}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-worke